{{Quote|Did&mdash; Did the rest of the family make it?''"<br />"''Yes. We were off-world when the attack happened. Your mother and I have been trying to contact you for days, Kazuda.|Kazuda and Hamato Xiono|audio=HamatoCalls-AQuickSalvageRun.flac|<ref name="A Quick Salvage Run" />}}
A [[Gender|female]] '''individual''' was the [[Parent|mother]] of [[Resistance]] [[spy]] [[Kazuda Xiono]]. They raised their son in a wealthy [[Xiono family|family]] on the [[New Republic]] [[capital]] [[planet]] [[Hosnian Prime]], alongside his father, [[senator]] of the New Republic [[Hamato Xiono]]. They, Hamato, and the rest of their family managed to survive the [[First Order]]'s [[Hosnian Cataclysm|destruction]] of Hosnian Prime and later attempted to make contact with their son.

==Biography==
{{Quote|Pay up, kid. That's 1,500 creds you owe me.''"<br />"''Well, I don't have that much on me, but if I could contact my parents&hellip;|Grevel and Kazuda Xiono|audio=GrevelHarassingKaz-TheRecruit.flac|<ref name="Recruit">{{Resistance|The Recruit}}</ref>}}
[[File:KazudaXiono-Card.png|thumb|left|200px|The mother of Kazuda Xiono (pictured) was part of a wealthy family.]]
The  of<ref name="A Quick Salvage Run" /> [[New Republic pilot]]<ref name="Recruit" /> [[Kazuda Xiono]] was a [[Gender|female]] member of the [[Xiono family]].<ref name="A Quick Salvage Run" /> They and Xiono's [[Parent|father]], the [[senator]] of the [[New Republic]] [[Hamato Xiono]], raised their son<ref name="KazData">{{Databank|kazuda-kaz-xiono|Kazuda "Kaz" Xiono}}</ref>&mdash;who was [[Reproduction|born]] in [[14 ABY]]<ref name="Kaz birth year">''[[Star Wars Resistance]]'' executive producer [[Athena Yvette Portillo]] stated Kazuda Xiono's age as twenty [[Standard year|years]] old at a [[Lucasfilm]] [https://web.archive.org/web/20190309054006/http://www.jedinews.co.uk/film-music-tv/articles/star-wars-is-back-on-tv-with-star-wars-resistance press event] ahead of the [[The Recruit|premiere]] of the show's [[Star Wars Resistance Season One|first season]]. ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' establishes that the events of [[Star Wars Resistance Season One|''Star Wars Resistance'' Season One]] take place in [[34 ABY]]. Since Kaz was twenty at that [[time]], he must have been [[Reproduction|born]] in [[14 ABY]].</ref>&mdash;as part of a wealthy family, living in the upper echelons<ref name="KazData" /> of the New Republic [[capital]] [[planet]]<ref name="USWNE">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref> [[Hosnian Prime]]'s aristocracy.<ref name="KazData" /> In [[34 ABY]],<ref name="RecruitDate">{{ResistanceDate|1|1}}</ref> while Kazuda was [[Mission on the Colossus platform|operating]] as a [[Resistance]] [[spy]] on the [[Trantor-class supertanker fuel depot|supertanker fuel depot]] known as the ''[[Colossus]]'', he accidentally threw a [[Holodarts|holodart]] into [[gorgmonger]] [[Bolza Grool]], which in turn prompted the [[Aleena]] [[Grevel]] to hassle the spy for 1,500 [[Galactic Credit Standard|credits]], claiming he had lost the game. Kazuda responded that he did not have enough on him but could ask his parents for [[Currency|money]].<ref name="Recruit" />

When the [[First Order]] [[Hosnian Cataclysm|destroyed]] Hosnian Prime<ref name="NoEscape1">{{Resistance|No Escape: Part 1}}</ref> that same year,<ref name="NoEscapeDate">{{ResistanceDate|1|20}}</ref> Kazuda's mother and Hamato, along with the rest of the family, survived, as they had been off-world during the attack. Kazuda's parents then began attempting to contact their son over the course of several [[Standard day|days]].<ref name="A Quick Salvage Run" /> However, Kazuda believed his family to be [[Death|dead]] because of the cataclysm.<ref name="NoEscape2">{{Resistance|No Escape: Part 2}}</ref> When Hamato finally made contact, he informed Kazuda via [[hologram]] that they had survived. He then warned his son that he had put the whole family in danger, for the First Order had identified him and could send [[bounty hunter]]s.<ref name="A Quick Salvage Run" /> Despite the threat to himself and his family, Kazuda resolved to continue serving the Resistance.<ref name="KazData" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|&hellip;we would have met his mother. We would have met his older sister. Essentially it would have been those characters that we would have met and we would have seen all of them are now sort of affiliated with the First Order out of sheer need to survive.|Brandon Auman, about proposed third season ''Star Wars Resistance'' pitches|audio=XionoMotherSisterFirstOrder-YouTube.flac|<ref name="Interview">{{WookYouTube|ML1nYpSU0d0|Wookieepedia Interviews - Brandon Auman}}</ref>}}
[[File:BrandonAuman.jpg|thumb|right|240px|Brandon Auman (pictured) and Justin Ridge made pitches to Lucasfilm about a potential third season of ''Star Wars Resistance'', which would have involved Kazuda's Xiono's mother.]]
The mother of Kazuda Xiono was first indirectly implied to exist in "[[The Recruit]],"<ref name="Recruit" /> the first episode of [[Star Wars Resistance Season One|first season]] of the animated television series ''[[Star Wars Resistance]]'', which first premiered on [[October 7]], [[2018]].<ref name="WDTVPress">{{DisneyPress|wdtv=1|url=disneychannel/shows/star-wars-resistance/episodes|text=Star Wars Resistance}}</ref> They were first explicitly mentioned in "[[A Quick Salvage Run]],"<ref name="A Quick Salvage Run" /> the second episode of ''Resistance''{{'s}} [[Star Wars Resistance Season Two|second season]], which premiered on [[October 13]], [[2019]].<ref name="WDTVPress" />

Early pitches about a potential third season for ''Star Wars Resistance'' by the show's executive producers [[Brandon Auman]] and [[Justin Ridge]] were discussed with [[Lucasfilm]]. In an interview, Auman reflected that one proposed plotline included meeting Kazuda's family again, including Hamato, the mother, and Kazuda's [[Kazuda Xiono's sister|older sister]]. The executive producer further elaborated that Hamato would have tried to have his son betray the Resistance for the First Order in an effort to keep him safe. However, Auman noted that Kazuda would have refused the offer, putting him at odds with the rest of his family&mdash;which included his mother&mdash;who were all affiliated with the First Order by that point to survive. However, ultimately, the production ceased after its second season.<ref name="Interview" />

